### Page 1: The gRPC Service Definition (`.proto`)

First, we need to define the interface. We will use `stream ServerStreaming` to send the output line-by-line as the Ansible playbook runs.

**File:** `playbook_service.proto`

```proto
syntax = "proto3";

package playbook;

// Represents a single line of output from Ansible
message PlaybookOutput {
  string timestamp = 1;
  string content = 2;
  string host = 3; // Optional: which host the line came from
}

// Request to start a playbook
message PlaybookRequest {
  string playbook_path = 1;
  map<string, string> extra_vars = 2;
  string inventory = 3;
}

// Service definition
service PlaybookService {
  // Runs the playbook and streams output back to the client
  rpc RunPlaybook (PlaybookRequest) returns (stream PlaybookOutput);
}
```

